// Title: OilRig APT Registry Persistence
// Sigma ID: 7bdf2a7c-3acc-4091-9581-0a77dad1c5b5
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Markus Neis, Jonhnathan Ribeiro, Daniil Yugoslavskiy, oscd.community
// Date: 2018-03-23 | Modified: 2023-03-08
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, defense-impairment, G0049, T1053.005, S0111, T1543.003, T1112, command-and-control, T1071.004
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects OilRig registry persistence as reported by Nyotron in their March 2018 report
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20180402134442/https://nyotron.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Nyotron-OilRig-Malware-Report-March-2018C.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2018/TA/OilRig/registry_event_apt_oilrig_mar18.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\UMe" or RegistryKey endswith "SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\UT"
